# Docker build context exclusions. ONE file, read by BOTH images in this repo:
# `Dockerfile` (the game + player image) and `Dockerfile.replay-viewer` (the
# wasm bundle `tools/build_replay_viewer.sh` builds).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE THAT BITES: nim.cfg
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both Dockerfiles do this, in this order:
#
#     WORKDIR /workspace/lux
#     COPY nimby.lock .
#     RUN nimby --global sync nimby.lock      # <-- WRITES /workspace/lux/nim.cfg
#     COPY . .                                # <-- overwrites it
#
# `nimby --global sync` does not only populate ~/.nimby/pkgs; it writes the
# resulting `--path:` lines into the WORKING DIRECTORY's nim.cfg ("# Created by
# Nimby", one `--path:"/root/.nimby/pkgs/<pkg>/src"` per dependency). That
# generated file is the only thing that puts bitworld & co. on the container's
# search path -- the Nim install's own config carries stdlib paths only.
#
# `nim.cfg` is .gitignore'd, so a fresh checkout has none and `COPY . .` leaves
# the generated one alone. A DEVELOPER's checkout has one, holding absolute
# paths into THEIR home directory, and `COPY . .` overwrites the generated file
# with it. Every path in it is then missing inside the container and the build
# dies on the first dependency import:
#
#     /workspace/lux/src/lux/global.nim(22, 16)
#       Error: cannot open file: bitworld/spriteprotocol
#
# CI never sees this (checkout@v5 gives it a clean tree, and the test job
# regenerates nim.cfg from the runner's own package tree), so the failure is
# local-only: it hits exactly the developer running ./tools/build_replay_viewer.sh
# on a machine that has ever built this repo natively.
nim.cfg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The rest of .gitignore: build products of a NATIVE host build. A macOS
# nimcache or Mach-O binary in an amd64 Linux context is at best dead weight
# and at worst a stale artifact the build might not overwrite.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (Docker's patterns are anchored at the context root and are NOT implicitly
# recursive the way git's are, so anything .gitignore matches at any depth
# needs an explicit `**/` here.)
dist/
replay-viewer/dist/
**/nimcache/
**/.nimcache*
**/*.exe
lux-ai
lux-ai-player

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local noise that is not in .gitignore because it never lands in the
# repo root of a clean checkout, but is present on a working machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.claude
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store

# CI/agent scratch written into the repo root by the viewer smoke harness.
viewer-smoke.png
viewer-smoke.json
fixture-out/
